IO-59: print a space before each flow value in the summary tables

The summary tables print flows with FlowFmt = "%9.2f" ("%9.3f" for MGD and
CMS), and the Node Inflow Summary prints the maximum lateral and maximum
total inflow back to back. A flow of 100,000.00 or more (10,000.000 in MGD
or CMS) fills the field, so it runs into the value before it, e.g.
"150000.00150000.00" for 150,000 GPM. Use " %8.2f" / " %8.3f": every
value that fits prints exactly as before, and a larger one is still
separated by a space. The 5.2.5 entry in the file header described a
change to scientific notation that was reverted (0d3fdbec); it now
describes this change.

Requires: IO-61

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after IO-61_swmm530.patch:
    git apply IO-59_swmm530.patch

